-## Payment and settlement boundary
+## Final settlement policy `FinalSettlementSnapshot-v1`
+
+`FinalSettlement` extends the existing run/revision/line/log aggregate; it does not create a second payroll writer. Calculate and Save require one available staff id and typed `finalSettlement` inputs: last working day in the selected month, joining/rejoining date, CalendarDays/Fixed30 day basis, reviewed remaining leave days and Basic/Gross basis, ticket quota/period/price/eligibility percentage, and reviewed earned gratuity days and Basic/Gross basis. Numeric inputs are required; an explicit zero is accepted for an inapplicable entitlement. The first joining date and designation remain source facts. No employment-status change is written.
+
+- Salary coverage is inclusive from the later of month start or actual joining through last working day. Latest salary packages are selected before last day + 1; salary changes within the covered period and recorded absences still block Save until their policy is resolved.
+- CalendarDays divides by actual month days. Fixed30 divides by 30 and caps covered salary days at 30. Basic and allowances are rounded separately and sum to Gross. Package earnings/deductions are prorated; recorded overtime and due installment deductions retain actual amounts.
+- Commission and sales incentive are disclosed once. Package LeaveEncashment/EndOfServiceBenefits components block double counting. Leave/gratuity = reviewed days × the disclosed rounded Basic/Gross daily rate. Ticket = quota × price × eligibility / 100. Quota period is recorded context; the system does not infer statutory or service-earned eligibility.
+- Total = normal salary + leave salary + ticket + gratuity. The saved line Additional includes commission and all settlement additions, preserving `Gross + Overtime + Additional - Deductions = NetPay`; the settlement snapshot separates the portions for review.
+- One final settlement root per employee across all months. Any other current saved payroll type containing the employee in the same month blocks another salary Save. Save rechecks guards inside its tenant lock/transaction; a unique filtered final index protects races.
+- Saved staff/month/last working day are immutable. Changed reviewed inputs create an unpaid revision and reset approval. Existing monthly policy and source hash shapes remain compatible. Historical typed JSON retains dates, bases, daily rates and breakdown independently of mutable staff data.
+
+## Pay slip reads
+
+`GET /PaySlips` projects current saved PayrollLine revisions with counted paging and exact date/no/type/staff filters. Columns are No, Name, Code, Date, Type, Total Amount and Status; identity/status fields are limited to the corresponding list DTO. The deterministic number is `runId-revisionNumber-staffId`; No searches the complete identifier. Date is inclusive month end for monthly payroll or the final last working day.
+
+`GET /PaySlips/{id}` reads exactly one historical PayrollLine.Id and its owning revision/root. Approval, payment and current/superseded state remain distinct; salary and final-settlement amounts are saved snapshots. `GET /PaySlips/staff` uses saved line identities, preserving historical employee choices. The service is covered by the existing scoped assembly scanner. No slip entity, amount write, payment toggle or journal endpoint is added. `/FinalSettlementProcess`, `/PaySlips` and their bilingual `/UserGuide/hrm` topics complete the frontend handoff.
+
+## Disbursement boundary
 
 Save and Approve do not mean payment. A separate disbursement owner must consume the current approved revision, record actual payment/ledger effects atomically, update installment payment state where applicable and append its operation log. No manual Paid toggle or actual payment writer exists in this change.
 
